On Mar 6, 1:24 pm, masquerade...@gmail.com wrote:
> I've heard mentions in many different places of intentionally avoiding
> fights and decreasing your own level as a strategy. This is a newbie
> question, but what is the advantage of limiting or decreasing your
> level, what classes should do it, and when?


Why: Monsters are generated based on your experience level (among
other things), so they stay easier as you go down hte dungeon.  also,
protection costs (much) less.

Who: best characters to avoid gaining levels with: Think about it this
way. You get xp for killing monsters. Some classes are poor at killing
monsters, but better at other things.  Ergo:

healer and tourist are good. (former probably better than the latter).


as far as when: If you're new, learning how to avoid fights and use
your pet is a good idea, as it will make you better in the long run as
well.   And naturally, the mass protection you can buy is quite nice.



